This product includes and builds upon the following third-party works:

1. Laya — Convai Innovations
   https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya
   Licensed under the Apache License 2.0.
   Laya-Vision extends Laya's decision model, training objective (RLCD) and
   request/response interface. The shipped base weights (weights/base/) are a
   fine-tune of the Laya checkpoint on the LocalLLaMA/typed-decisions dataset,
   produced by the upstream fine-tuning recipe. No files in the Laya package
   are modified.

2. SigLIP — google/siglip-base-patch16-384, Google
   https://huggingface.co/google/siglip-base-patch16-384
   Licensed under the Apache License 2.0.
   Used unmodified as a frozen vision encoder; downloaded at runtime, not
   redistributed here.

3. ModernBERT — Answer.AI / LightOn (encoder architecture used by Laya)
   Licensed under the Apache License 2.0.

4. RVL-CDIP dataset — Harley, Ufkes and Derpanis (2015)
   https://huggingface.co/datasets/aharley/rvl_cdip
   "Evaluation of Deep Convolutional Nets for Document Image Classification and
   Retrieval", ICDAR 2015. Derived from the IIT-CDIP Test Collection (Legacy
   Tobacco Document Library). Distributed for research use; the trained weights
   in this release inherit that context. No images from the dataset are
   redistributed here.

5. Tesseract OCR — Google and contributors
   Licensed under the Apache License 2.0. Used at runtime for the optional
   text channel; not redistributed.

6. Qwen2-VL-2B-Instruct — Alibaba Cloud
   Licensed under the Apache License 2.0. Used only during development for the
   Route A baseline and label-generation experiments; not part of the release.
